{"findings":[{"rule_id":"MF-005","evidence":[{"kind":"title_block","ref":"heat_treatment","page":1,"quote":"---"},{"kind":"note","ref":"N2","page":1,"quote":"HEAT TREATMENT :- 1) TO BE TOUGHENED UPTO 24-32 HRC. 2) RETAPPING TO BE DONE AFTER SURFACE TREATMENT AT SUPPLIER END.( IF APPLICABLE )"}],"comment":"The title block heat treatment field is '---' while note N2 specifies hardening to 24-32 HRC but does not state at which manufacturing stage the heat treatment applies (e.g., before or after final machining). This ambiguity can cause the machinist to machine hardened stock or leave insufficient stock for post-treatment finishing. The designer should fill in the heat treatment field and add the process stage to note N2."

,"recommended_correction":"Update the heat treatment title block field and revise N2 to specify when the toughening is to be performed relative to machining and surface treatment."},{"rule_id":"MF-007","evidence":[{"kind":"title_block","ref":"material","page":1,"quote":"#"},{"kind":"note","ref":"N3","page":1,"quote":"NOTE : # MATERIAL : EN-91 # FINISH : E.N.P. # MACHINING :"}],"comment":"The title block material field contains only '#' instead of a valid material designation, while note N3 names 'EN-91'. This conflict means the procurement system reading the title block will not know what material to order. The designer should enter the correct material specification in the title block material field."

,"recommended_correction":"Replace '#' in the title block material field with the actual material specification consistent with note N3."}]}
